    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Scorn Fate",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "curse",
        "misfortune",
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "The path maiden targets a creature she can see. The creature must attempt a DC 32 Will save save. On a failure, the creature's next roll is cursed. If the result of the roll is a critical success, it becomes a regular success. A success becomes a failure, and a failure becomes a critical failure. That creature is then temporarily immune to Scorn Fate for 24 hours."
    },
    {
      "kind": "ability",
      "name": "Vengeful Frenzy",
      "actions": 2,
      "category": "offensive",
      "traits": [
        "emotion",
        "mental",
        "occult"
      ],
      "text": "The path maiden targets a creature within 60 feet that she can see. The target must attempt a DC 32 Will save save against the path maiden's spell DC. On a failure, the target is Confused until the end of its next turn, but it can't attack path maidens or itself as the result of this confusion."
    },
    {
      "kind": "spell",
      "name": "Create Undead",
      "rank": 2,
      "ref": "spells:spell/create-undead"
    }
  ],
  "text": "Worshippers in Shenmen who devote their every breath to Pharasma only to defy the goddess with their last sometimes transform, upon death, into path maidens. The garments all path maidens wear are the last vestiges of their former faith, a permanent reminder of their disgrace.\n\nPath Nomads\n\nPath maidens almost always manifest in feminine forms. Those who manifest in masculine forms are instead known as path nomads. These undead have the same abilities but tend to travel more widely; they represent turning one's back on Pharasma's role as a prophet and manipulator of destiny than of her roles over birth and death."
